    "durationMs": 178084,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: NestJS 11 + TypeORM (`@nestjs/typeorm`, the idiomatic Nest persistence layer) + PostgreSQL 16 via `DATABASE_URL`, with class-validator DTOs and a global exception filter that normalizes all error responses to `{\"error\": ...}` (including mapping body-parser/400 errors to 422).\n\n**Structure**: `src/links/` (entity, DTO, service, controller), `src/database/` (data source + migration), `src/common/global-http-exception.filter.ts`. The `links` table has `id`, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`.\n\n**Key behaviors, all tested with curl:**\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`; URL stored and returned unchanged; generated codes are random 7-char strings from the allowed alphabet; duplicate custom code → 409 (via pre-check + unique-violation catch, race-safe)\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 / 404; `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with Location, using an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 ... RETURNING url` so clicks increment exactly once per request (verified 3 redirects → clicks: 3)\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}` in creation order\n- 422 with `error` field for malformed JSON, missing/invalid URL (non-absolute, ftp, no host, non-string), and invalid codes (short, long, bad chars)\n- Restart persistence confirmed: killed the server, re-ran `sh start.sh` (migrations idempotent), all links and click counts survived\n\n**Notes**: `sh start.sh` runs the migration then serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` (verified reachable via the container's external IP). Dependencies are installed already — the environment has `omit=dev` npm config, so I put the `@types/*` packages in regular dependencies. The database is left empty and clean; README documents startup."
